648	/// openai-node `ChatCompletionStream`: choices and tool calls are SPARSE arrays by index;
649	/// `id`, `type`, `function.name` and `custom.name` are REPLACED when truthy; `arguments` is
650	/// appended when not null, `custom.input` when truthy. A legacy `function_call` object is taken as
651	/// is, then its name replaced and its arguments appended. `finalChatCompletion` raises when a
652	/// choice has no `finish_reason` or no `role`, a tool call has no `type`, or a name or arguments
653	/// are missing. The SSE layer stops at `[DONE]` and raises on an `error` event or a truthy
654	/// `error` field.
